// §3.3 — `is_empty`. Parameter flows through match (read),
// not to the return.
//
//   Expected disposition (post-Track-1-Phase-2): Borrowed.
//   Reachability fact today: UnusedParametersLens reports the
//   parameter as USED (the body matches on it), but the return
//   value is independent of `b`'s payload.
//
// Abstraction boundary probed: "no reach from return, match-read
// only".
//
// Shape note: §3.3 writes this against `List<Int>` with
// `Empty | Cons(p)`. Two adaptations needed for today's lowering:
//
//   1. The match-on-List core-type lowering is not yet wired
//      (the shape lands with a later slice of substrate work), so
//      the fixture substitutes an equivalent user sum — same
//      abstraction (match-read-only, param inspected not
//      forwarded).
//   2. The names `is_empty` and `Empty` both appear in
//      `src/v3/std/list.dag`; using them at fixture top-level
//      would collide with the stdlib. The fixture renames to
//      `is_empty_fx` / `Nil` so the collision doesn't shadow
//      what the test is actually probing.
//
// When the List match lowering lands and name-scoping allows
// shadowing the stdlib names, the canonical §3.3 form can be
// swapped in without the test interface changing.
type BoxedFx = BoxedV(Int) | Nil
fn is_empty_fx(b: BoxedFx) -> Bool = match b { BoxedV(v) => false, Nil => true }
let sample: Bool = is_empty_fx(Nil)
